From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:00:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Release utility futures when callers stop waiting

Base: candidate-39 plus request-submission cleanup (0cff1109940f15d08f2e893ae06e0a527fde438a). The affected utility code is unchanged in candidate-38.

Rationale: encoding errors, failed sends and cancellations before any reply can leave entries in utility_results indefinitely. Bound each entry to its caller lifetime and tolerate late responses. Handle the synchronous cancellation race without stopping the output receiver.

Quality: preserve utility results and original exceptions; decoding and GPU work are unchanged. Tests cover all send stages, cancellation, repetition, late replies, concurrent callers and ordinary success/error responses.

Upstream status: local, not submitted.
---
